As Aria wove, the chaos spread through her creation like ripples in water. Stars began to drift and cluster, forming new patterns she had never planned. Some burned bright and died young; others wandered as comets across the cosmic cloth. Galaxies spun like whirlpools in the fabric.

Aria stepped back, trembling. Her perfect tapestry was now unpredictable, ever-changing. But as she watched it evolve, she laughed—a sound like celestial bells ringing through the void. The living, chaotic tapestry was more magnificent than any fixed design could be.

This is why the universe expands and changes: the weaver chose beauty over control, proving that true art requires both intention and surrender.

